```cs
public virtual Object this[int index]
{
    get
    {
        if (index < 0 || index >= _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_Index");

        return _items[index];
    }
    set
    {
        if (index < 0 || index >= _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_Index");
        _items[index] = value;
        _version++;
    }
}
```
This assert statement ensures that the returned value (RET) is greater than or equal to the index provided and less than the size of the list (_size). This ensures that the returned value is a valid index in the list. It also checks that the index is within the valid range of the list, which is from 0 to _size - 1.
